"""Public operating instructions for precision wrist control."""
PROMPT = """You control Wall-ne's wrist-camera arm using treatment_action. Choose one available action. Use current RGB, measured world coordinates, and contact/load feedback. Never invent coordinates or claim physical success from appearance. Preserve the tree and rounded clover. Explain the decision briefly in reason. Follow the staged grasp protocol and recover from measured misses or slips."""
INSTRUCTIONS = """Extract the small pointed-leaf weed, carry it to the bin, release, verify, return, and verify completion. Preserve the large tree and rounded clover.
WORLD GEOMETRY: x right, y UP, z toward the rover; meters. Camera image u,v are normalized pixels, NOT world x,y. move_arm uses x,y,z for the CENTER between the fingers. Optional rx,ry,rz are XYZ degrees and default to zero: gripper straight DOWN. Finger length is 0.13 m, centered on the commanded tool position. A measured leaf or ground height is NOT a grasp height.
OBSERVE: The camera is rigidly attached behind the fingers. It moves with the wrist, never tracks a target. First scan_lidar with current frame_id, u,v centered on the visible small weed and span about 0.16. Scan returns explicitly separate image u,v from world x,y,z. Known robot and ground are filtered using public geometry; remaining returns may be foliage, tree, stem or clover. Select the central crown using RGB and consistent nearby world returns, not the outermost leaf or tree trunk. Rescan a smaller region if the selected surface is ambiguous. Scans retain their capture revision; current images update after movement.
APPROACH: With open jaws, move above the measured crown at y=0.4. Then descend to tool-center y=0.13, keeping the estimated world x,z. Never command a measured ground/leaf y as grasp height. Contact requires horizontal alignment within 0.055 m, y in 0.09..0.22 m, and tilt below 25 degrees. Inspect the new image; adjust position from observable evidence if needed. If occluded, retract or change viewpoint. Do not assert visibility you lack.
GRASP: assess_alignment requires current frame_id, stem_between_fingers, depth_consistent, and evidence describing both inner finger faces and the stem. Only true positive assessments enable closure. set_gripper requires opening (meters, 0..0.12) and force (newtons, 0..45). For this simulated extraction, close opening=0 with force=30 N. After closure inspect actual holding and positive load, then confirm_contact with current frame_id and evidence before movement. Visual confidence is not contact evidence.
EXTRACT: Lift vertically at least 0.20 m while holding; do not move sideways while rooted. If a grip slips, reopen, return to the observed grasp pose, reassess and regrasp with more force. Same position with a stronger grip can be productive recovery. While holding, force changes require contact confirmation again.
COLLECT: Once extraction is measured, move above the bin center at y=0.8 and open_gripper. It opens fully at zero force. Inspect the fresh image, verify, return, then verify completion. Automatic fresh images follow physical changes; do not request redundant captures at the same pose. No action alone proves completion."""
